 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
 - Monocular ambiguity: Scale drift is a common issue in monocular SLAM, though the sources do not specify MonoGS's specific scale-fixing mechanism [S1].
-- Degenerate input: Lack of texture or rapid motion may break photometric consistency [S1].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
 **Time and Memory Complexity:**
 - The method is designed for online streaming, with the streaming time dominated by motion tracking, refinement, and structure updates rather than rendering ($t_{\text{stream}} \approx t_{\text{motion}} + t_{\text{refine}} + t_{\text{structure}} \gg t_{\text{render}}$) [S1].
-- Measured performance on Replica office0 (12 RGB-D frames, though MonoGS is monocular, this benchmark is used for comparison): Wrapped time is 2250.57 ms/frame (0.444 frames/s), trajectory error is 0.000082 m, and model size is 2.14 MiB [S1].
